# Keep Node-only files out of the Apps Script project. Patterns are relative to
# rootDir.
#
# THE RULE IS THE EXTENSION, deliberately: every real Apps Script file in
# connectors/gas/ is `.gs` (plus appsscript.json), and every Node-only file —
# the test suite, its fixtures — is `.js`. So `**/*.js` covers the category, not
# a list of names.
#
# This used to be `**/test_code.js` + `**/*.test.js`, i.e. two exact names. On
# 2026-08-24 that let connectors/gas/fixtures_mayers_ocr.js (a Node module
# ending in `module.exports = {...}`) push to GAS, where `module` is undefined.
# Apps Script evaluates every top-level statement in the project on ANY
# execution, so one stray `module.exports` threw `ReferenceError: module is not
# defined` out of doGet — taking down the whole /exec endpoint, which is the
# sole ingest path. Deployed v29, caught by the post-deploy probe, rolled back
# to v28. A name-based ignore cannot see the next such file coming.
**/*.js

# Harness artifacts must never reach the Apps Script project. .clasp.json sets
# skipSubdirectories:false and jsonExtensions:[".json"], so a step*-red-check.json
# written with the wrong cwd under rootDir would otherwise be pushed live.
**/phases/**
**/*.log
**/*.md
